# `.dockerignore` — what must never enter the build context (PLAN.md §11.1, §9.5).
#
# **Depth matters, and the first two versions of this file got it wrong.** Docker's matching is
# *not* `.gitignore`'s: a pattern is matched against the path relative to the context root, and `*`
# does not cross a `/`. Measured on real builds:
#
#   * a bare `*.pem` excluded `./private.pem` and kept `./sub/private.pem` — a private key inside
#     the image;
#   * a bare `__pycache__/` let `migrations/__pycache__` and `scripts/__pycache__` ship;
#   * a bare `build/`, `dist/`, `venv/`, `htmlcov/` and `.coverage` did the same for
#     `scripts/build/…`, `scripts/dist/…`, `scripts/venv/…`, `scripts/htmlcov/…` and
#     `scripts/.coverage`;
#   * `id_rsa` had **no pattern at all**, although `scripts/audit_image.py` treats it as forbidden
#     by name — the two disagreed.
#
# Every pattern that has to match at any depth therefore carries a `**/` prefix. The root-level
# spellings are kept as well where they existed, because they cost nothing and make the intent
# obvious. `tests/integration/test_dockerignore.py` builds probe contexts and checks the result
# **with Docker itself**, and it builds a stripped variant to prove the check can fail.

.git
.gitignore

# --- Secrets and keys: the reason this file exists ---------------------------- #
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
service-account*.json
id_rsa
id_rsa*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/service-account*.json
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa*

# --- Test and tooling artefacts ------------------------------------------------ #
# `scripts/` is deliberately NOT excluded: the migrator, the webhook registrar and the Ollama
# compatibility probe ship in the image, so an operator can run them without a checkout.
tests/
**/tests/
docs/
**/docs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage.xml

# --- Build residue -------------------------------------------------------------- #
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# --- Planning documents (not part of the runtime image) ------------------------- #
PLAN.md
PLAN-REVIEW-LOG.md
PROJECT_SPEC.md
.claude/
